From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:13:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/27] feat(webhooks): limit hooks to canvases, name the
 element, manage them from the operator API
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A comment webhook fired for every canvas its owner could open, and its payload did not say
which element a pinned comment is on, so a receiver watching one board had to filter every
event and look the element up itself. Instances that hide the Settings pane also had no way
to set a hook at all.

- webhooks.canvas_ids (jsonb, default [], migration 0051): the canvases a hook fires for;
  empty keeps the old behaviour, every canvas the owner can open. Each listed canvas must
  exist and pass the same durable-access check delivery uses (at most 50), checked again on
  every delivery, so losing access to a listed canvas silences it there.
- publicComment carries elementId (the element's data-doop-id, null for frame and canvas
  comments) and snippet (the element's markup at comment time, null when none).
- Operator API: GET/POST /api/operator/users/:user/webhooks, PATCH and DELETE
  /users/:user/webhooks/:hookId, POST …/:hookId/test. Same validation as the session routes
  (shared zod schemas, WebhookInputError → 400), the signing secret returned once on create,
  every write logged as [operator]. PATCH covers enable/disable, since a hook pauses itself
  after repeated failures.

The Settings pane does not edit canvasIds yet; a hook made there stays all-canvases.

Tests: webhooks.test.ts (canvas limits and checks, payload fields), operator.test.ts (end to
end: an agent's add_comment over MCP reaches a receiver for the listed canvas only, with
elementId and snippet; disable, test, widen, delete).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
